From: AztecBot <tech@aztec-labs.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 19:02:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(pxe): charge the teardown call's AVM startup gas in
 kernelless simulation

The private kernel's gas meter charges FIXED_AVM_STARTUP_L2_GAS for the teardown call on top of its gas limits, because the AVM dispatches it like any other enqueued public call. Kernelless simulation is what gas estimation runs on, so it has to meter the same amount: otherwise the estimated gas limits of a tx with a teardown call fall short of the gas_used the kernel proves, and the tx is rejected for exceeding its limits.

diff --git a/yarn-project/pxe/src/contract_function_simulator/contract_function_simulator.ts b/yarn-project/pxe/src/contract_function_simulator/contract_function_simulator.ts
index 981af63e696762cfdb8447815907d17ea88b4205..7d4edaa16d914d05ef417e8263145cb2d44453b0 100644
--- a/yarn-project/pxe/src/contract_function_simulator/contract_function_simulator.ts
+++ b/yarn-project/pxe/src/contract_function_simulator/contract_function_simulator.ts
@@ -725,7 +725,12 @@ export async function generateSimulatedProvingResult(
     );
     gasUsed = meterGasUsed(revertibleData, isPrivateOnlyTx).add(meterGasUsed(nonRevertibleData, isPrivateOnlyTx));
     if (publicTeardownCallRequest) {
-      gasUsed = gasUsed.add(privateExecutionResult.entrypoint.publicInputs.txContext.gasSettings.teardownGasLimits);
+      // The teardown call is dispatched by the AVM like any other enqueued public call, so it consumes the startup
+      // gas on top of its gas limits.
+      const teardownStartupGas = Gas.from({ daGas: 0, l2Gas: FIXED_AVM_STARTUP_L2_GAS });
+      gasUsed = gasUsed
+        .add(privateExecutionResult.entrypoint.publicInputs.txContext.gasSettings.teardownGasLimits)
+        .add(teardownStartupGas);
     }
 
     inputsForPublic = new PartialPrivateTailPublicInputsForPublic(
